WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
"You can't destroy Magica!" Perda cried to Morb.

2
00:00:03.921 --> 00:00:07.481
She turned to Wyssa. "You have to stop him!"

3
00:00:07.482 --> 00:00:11.395
Wyssa said nothing. She was staring at the contraption in horror.

4
00:00:11.396 --> 00:00:16.575
"It's too late," Morb sneered. "No one can stop me now!"

5
00:00:16.576 --> 00:00:23.183
Zann stared at his parents. Their bodies twitched as the memory mice scampered over them.

6
00:00:23.184 --> 00:00:27.641
"Are the mice really sucking out my parents' memories?" he asked.

7
00:00:27.642 --> 00:00:31.568
"That's right, boy," Morb said. "But don't worry.

8
00:00:31.569 --> 00:00:37.790
Once their memories are emptied, I'll have no further use for your parents. You can have them back."

9
00:00:37.791 --> 00:00:44.092
Zann shuddered. He'd never imagined there could be anything worse than being separated from his parents.

10
00:00:44.093 --> 00:00:52.047
Now he wasn't so sure. He couldn't stand the thought of finding them just in time to watch them forget everything.

11
00:00:52.048 --> 00:00:54.971
Would they remember their old home in First City?

12
00:00:54.972 --> 00:00:58.237
Or that family vacation they'd all taken to the Flower Forest?

13
00:00:58.238 --> 00:01:00.357
Would they even remember him

14
00:01:00.358 --> 00:01:05.927
? Morb turned to the Roodian queen. "I'm glad you're here to witness this," he

15
00:01:05.928 --> 00:01:09.668
taunted. "Without you, it never could have

16
00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:13.697
happened." Still thinking about the past, Zann stared at his

17
00:01:13.698 --> 00:01:18.762
parents. Then he noticed a couple of memory mice sniffing curiously in his

18
00:01:18.763 --> 00:01:24.491
direction. He looked over at Wyssa. "How do people invite the mice to eat their memories?" he

19
00:01:24.492 --> 00:01:30.079
whispered. She appeared confused. "Simply by opening their minds to

20
00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:33.182
them." "Good." Zann glanced at his friends and

21
00:01:33.183 --> 00:01:36.528
Venna. "Start thinking about Magica," he

22
00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.895
whispered. "Any memories you can come up

23
00:01:38.896 --> 00:01:41.247
with. And invite the mice to come to

24
00:01:41.248 --> 00:01:47.661
you." "What?" Perda looked alarmed. "You mean ask those things to eat our

25
00:01:47.662 --> 00:01:53.100
memories?" Zann nodded. "There are five of us, and only two of my parents," he

26
00:01:53.101 --> 00:01:55.998
said. "Maybe we can draw the mice

27
00:01:55.999 --> 00:02:00.342
away!" Morb glanced over. "What are you whispering about over there?" he

28
00:02:00.343 --> 00:02:03.684
snapped. "You should be grateful that you're here to see

29
00:02:03.685 --> 00:02:08.231
this. Otherwise you'd have only moments to live." He

30
00:02:08.232 --> 00:02:12.776
smirked. "Of course, I can't guarantee you have much longer than

31
00:02:12.777 --> 00:02:16.995
that. The Beast of the Otherworld is always

32
00:02:16.996 --> 00:02:20.901
hungry." Zann ignored Morb and focused his thoughts on

33
00:02:20.902 --> 00:02:28.306
home. As more and more memories flooded his mind, Zann tried to send them toward the mice, inviting them to

34
00:02:28.307 --> 00:02:34.836
share. One mouse wiggled its nose. Then it jumped down from Zann's father and took a step toward

35
00:02:34.837 --> 00:02:37.845
Zann. A second mouse followed, and then a

36
00:02:37.846 --> 00:02:43.552
third. Soon all the mice were scampering across the room, headed for Zann and his

37
00:02:43.553 --> 00:02:51.377
friends. "N-now what?" Gliss asked nervously, backing away as far as the troll restraining her would let

38
00:02:51.378 --> 00:02:55.583
her. Once again Morb had turned away to taunt the Roodian

39
00:02:55.584 --> 00:03:02.592
queen. When he finally noticed the memory mice moving away from his machine, he let out a howl of

40
00:03:02.593 --> 00:03:07.057
fury. "To me!" Wyssa intoned at the same

41
00:03:07.058 --> 00:03:14.546
time. Zann held his breath as Wyssa's spell grabbed his parents and dragged them over to join the others.

42
00:03:14.547 --> 00:03:21.745
A split second later, the trolls were flung against the walls, and a Shield spell appeared around the rest of the group.

43
00:03:21.746 --> 00:03:25.689
"No!" Morb flung a bolt of energy at Wyssa.

44
00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:30.758
But it bounced off the glowing shield and ricocheted around the room.

45
00:03:30.759 --> 00:03:34.914
Zann hardly noticed. His parents looked dazed and weak.

46
00:03:34.915 --> 00:03:39.920
They stared at him blankly, and for a moment he was afraid it was too late.

47
00:03:39.921 --> 00:03:49.172
Then his mother's eyes brightened. "Zann?" she whispered, reaching out to touch his face. "Is it really you?"

48
00:03:49.173 --> 00:03:54.703
Zann's father smiled feebly. "We've missed you so much, son."

49
00:03:54.704 --> 00:03:58.059
"They remember you!" Perda exclaimed.

50
00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:03.888
"Of course we do," Zann's mother said. "But my head feels so fuzzy . . ."

51
00:04:03.889 --> 00:04:10.549
"You're lucky. The mice probably didn't focus on any particular memory," Wyssa told Zann's parents.

52
00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.995
"They just nibbled away here and there.

53
00:04:12.996 --> 00:04:18.105
You two will be weak for a while, but your memories should come back."

54
00:04:18.106 --> 00:04:21.141
Zann finally looked out through the shield.

55
00:04:21.142 --> 00:04:27.356
Morb was gnashing his teeth and stalking back and forth, occasionally blasting a troll.

56
00:04:27.357 --> 00:04:32.158
"It's not enough!" he cried. "I still don't have enough power!"

57
00:04:32.159 --> 00:04:35.848
"He's right. Look!" Perda pointed to the tube.

58
00:04:35.849 --> 00:04:39.515
The glowing energy stopped just short of the top.

59
00:04:39.516 --> 00:04:43.930
Morb snarled and then climbed into the machine!

60
00:04:43.931 --> 00:04:47.246
"Even a Void has memories," he hissed.

61
00:04:47.247 --> 00:04:51.124
"I suppose mine will work just as well as any.

62
00:04:51.125 --> 00:04:56.699
I have a few childhood memories I wouldn't mind getting rid of!"

63
00:04:56.700 --> 00:05:00.012
Venna gasped. "We have to do something!"

64
00:05:00.013 --> 00:05:03.167
"Stand back," Wyssa said grimly.

65
00:05:03.168 --> 00:05:06.252
She waved a hand, and the shield disappeared.

66
00:05:06.253 --> 00:05:13.348
Wyssa sent a huge Blast spell flying toward the contraption. But it stopped short, fizzling away.

67
00:05:13.349 --> 00:05:16.198
"It's not working!" Gliss cried.

68
00:05:16.199 --> 00:05:18.848
"I can see that, girl," Wyssa snapped.

69
00:05:18.849 --> 00:05:22.606
"The power of the Horns is blocking all magic."

70
00:05:22.607 --> 00:05:29.197
"Maybe I can still get through." Darb handed the mibbit to Gliss and then rushed toward the machine.

71
00:05:29.198 --> 00:05:32.352
But some unseen force bounced him back.

72
00:05:32.353 --> 00:05:35.033
He landed on the stone floor with a grunt.

73
00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:41.564
Venna paled. "There's no way to stop him! Magica is doomed!"

74
00:05:41.565 --> 00:05:44.763
Morb cackled as the mice continued to feed.

75
00:05:44.764 --> 00:05:49.353
His body slumped weakly, but his eyes glittered with triumph.

76
00:05:49.354 --> 00:05:51.791
"How do you like that?" he spat.

77
00:05:51.792 --> 00:05:59.179
"It took a Void to figure out how to focus enough magic energy to destroy Magica." He grinned nastily.

78
00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:08.124
"Then again, who else but a Void could really appreciate the true power of magic energy? Others take it for granted.

79
00:06:08.125 --> 00:06:17.288
But I could see how something that's harmless when used for small spells can be devastating when used for large ones!"

80
00:06:17.289 --> 00:06:20.091
"What are we going to do?" Perda cried.

81
00:06:20.092 --> 00:06:25.420
Zann didn't answer. All he could do was watch as the tube filled to the top.

82
00:06:25.421 --> 00:06:29.647
Morb brushed the mice off himself and got out of the machine.

83
00:06:29.648 --> 00:06:38.749
His mouth curled into an evil smile as he flung the hatch open.

